essbook><name>MATSUMURA, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a 1,4-methano-1,4,4a,9a-tetrahydrofluorene composition in which the contents of two cyclopentadiene trimers each having a specific structure are regulated to 100 to 5,000 ppm, which comprises reacting cyclopentadiene and/or dicyclopentadiene with 2 to 50 mol of indene per mol of the diene with heating and purifying the reaction product by distillation. By using the composition as a feed material for various polymerizations, gelation in polymerization is inhibited and resins having excellent optical properties can be obtained.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production d'une composition de 1,4-méthano-1,4,4a,9a-tétrahydrofluorène dans laquelle les contenus de deux trimères de cyclopentadiène, ayant chacun une structure spécifique, sont régulés entre 100 et 5000 ppm, consistant à faire réagir le cyclopentadiène et du dicyclopentadiène avec 2 à 50 mol d'indène par mole du diène, avec chauffage et purification du produit de réaction par distillation. L'utilisation de la composition comme matériau d'alimentation pour diverses polymérisations permet d'empêcher la gélification en polymérisation et d'obtenir des résines ayant d'excellentes propriétés optiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal